==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sniper the Heavy''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Sniper the Deadeye''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Sniper the Recruit has a very long-ranged attack. His stats are almost non-existent, but his knockback ability is particularly useful when stacked. He is essentially a free [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]], albeit with lower damage. Like Sniper the Cat, he is particularly useful against individual bosses (such as [[Dober P.D]] and [[Relic Bun-Bun]]). However, you should not use Sniper on levels with many peons, as he will likely miss the boss.

Sniper also works very well with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]], as one can delay enemies whilst the other helps to regain ground. Sniper can even knock enemies back into Cyberpunk's range in case they slip out.

==='''True Form'''===
Sniper the Deadeye performs much better with the extra range, the slow ability and faster attacks, but still has the weaknesses of his prior forms. In other words, unlocking this evolution simply makes him even better at what he already does.

